WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.223 --> 00:00:01.974
Great to be here in America.

00:00:01.974 --> 00:00:04.126
I just moved here, I'm Canadian.

00:00:04.126 --> 00:00:06.239
(audience cheers)

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:10.406
Ah, nice, yeah, no, but I just
moved here a few months ago,

00:00:10.429 --> 00:00:14.086
I looked at the current political climate

00:00:14.086 --> 00:00:16.055
and I said, "Now's the time."

00:00:16.055 --> 00:00:18.321
(audience laughs)

00:00:18.321 --> 00:00:19.238
Felt right.

00:00:20.845 --> 00:00:22.394
I just earned an interesting law.

00:00:22.394 --> 00:00:25.649
You know, up until
recently, it was illegal

00:00:25.649 --> 00:00:28.863
for gay men to donate blood in America,

00:00:28.863 --> 00:00:31.637
which is not cool, that's discrimination,

00:00:31.637 --> 00:00:33.674
but they changed the law
recently where gay men

00:00:33.674 --> 00:00:36.808
are now allowed to donate
blood, which is great news.

00:00:36.808 --> 00:00:40.756
There's just one little caveat,
gay men can now donate blood

00:00:40.756 --> 00:00:44.744
as long as they haven't
had sex in one year, so.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.697
(audience laughs)

00:00:46.697 --> 00:00:49.343
That's even more ridiculous, that's crazy.

00:00:49.343 --> 00:00:52.430
If you're not having
sex for one whole year,

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:55.083
that's a lifestyle choice
I can't get behind.

00:00:55.083 --> 00:00:57.639
(audience laughs)

00:00:57.639 --> 00:00:59.712
I have no problem getting
a blood transfusion

00:00:59.712 --> 00:01:02.314
from a gay man but I'll
be damned if I have

00:01:02.314 --> 00:01:04.505
loser blood coursing through my veins.

00:01:04.505 --> 00:01:06.714
(audience laughs)

00:01:06.714 --> 00:01:07.569
No way.

00:01:07.569 --> 00:01:11.206
(audience applauds)

00:01:11.206 --> 00:01:14.016
I'm not gay myself, I'm a straight man.

00:01:14.016 --> 00:01:16.572
I live with my girlfriend
and she's a sweetheart.

00:01:16.572 --> 00:01:18.887
She's had to make a few
adjustments 'cause I wear

00:01:18.887 --> 00:01:21.861
hearing aids, and I'm sure
you can see them, right?

00:01:21.861 --> 00:01:24.424
Got 'em here, yeah, I'm sure you can.

00:01:24.424 --> 00:01:26.257
If you can't see them,
get your eyes checked,

00:01:26.257 --> 00:01:27.843
(all laugh)

00:01:27.843 --> 00:01:30.203
you bunch of blind losers, but um,

00:01:30.203 --> 00:01:31.464
(audience laughs)

00:01:31.464 --> 00:01:34.393
no, but I hate all
other disabilities, and.

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:37.226
(audience laughs)

00:01:40.942 --> 00:01:42.857
The biggest adjustment my
girlfriend's had to make

00:01:42.857 --> 00:01:45.790
is I take my hearing aids
out when I go to sleep,

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:49.133
so, you know, when we're lying
in bed at the end of the day,

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:53.300
there's no casual transitions
from talking into sleeping.

00:01:53.845 --> 00:01:57.383
(audience laughs)

00:01:57.383 --> 00:02:00.596
When I take these hearing aids
out, talking time is over.

00:02:00.596 --> 00:02:02.669
(audience laughs)

00:02:02.669 --> 00:02:04.669
Sleeping time has begun.

00:02:06.153 --> 00:02:07.853
We even have a little ritual we do now

00:02:07.853 --> 00:02:11.333
where before I take them
out, I make like a last call.

00:02:11.333 --> 00:02:14.166
(audience laughs)

00:02:17.879 --> 00:02:22.046
I'm like, hey, baby, you got
any final thoughts on the day?

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:26.317
Any closing remarks 'cause I'm
about to shut this shit down.

00:02:26.502 --> 00:02:29.914
(audience laughs)

00:02:29.914 --> 00:02:31.223
it's not all fun and games though.

00:02:31.223 --> 00:02:34.152
She said something to me
recently that shook me,

00:02:34.152 --> 00:02:35.612
you know, rocked me to my very core.

00:02:35.612 --> 00:02:38.211
She said, "When we go to sleep at night,

00:02:38.211 --> 00:02:39.794
"when you take out your hearing aids,

00:02:39.794 --> 00:02:42.627
"I feel alone, I feel very alone,"

00:02:43.739 --> 00:02:47.324
and I was like, whoa, alone,
baby, no, you're not alone.

00:02:47.324 --> 00:02:50.501
Remember that I'm right there beside you,

00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:52.575
and if anything happens in
the middle of the night,

00:02:52.575 --> 00:02:56.077
anything at all, I need you to save me.

00:02:56.077 --> 00:02:58.910
(audience laughs)

00:03:00.188 --> 00:03:03.876
You're not alone, don't ever forget that.

00:03:03.876 --> 00:03:05.483
I need you so bad.

00:03:05.483 --> 00:03:08.745
(audience laughs)

00:03:08.745 --> 00:03:10.004
in fact, I'm going to need you to start

00:03:10.004 --> 00:03:14.032
sleeping with your contacts in, please.

00:03:14.032 --> 00:03:15.618
We're very vulnerable right now.

00:03:15.618 --> 00:03:18.451
(audience laughs)

00:03:20.422 --> 00:03:21.519
I take out my hearing aids,

00:03:21.519 --> 00:03:24.679
you take out your contacts, eww, you know.

00:03:24.679 --> 00:03:27.372
As a unit, we've gone full Helen Keller.

00:03:27.372 --> 00:03:30.372
(audience applauds)

00:03:34.729 --> 00:03:35.993
I don't hear whispering at all.

00:03:35.993 --> 00:03:38.682
Even with my hearing aids in,
whenever somebody whispers

00:03:38.682 --> 00:03:41.978
to me, I'm like, if this is a secret,

00:03:41.978 --> 00:03:45.145
you can rest assured, very, very safe.

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:51.701
Stays with us, mainly with you.

00:03:51.701 --> 00:03:53.250
(audience laughs)

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:55.487
It's the worst, I'm missing
out on all the good stuff,

00:03:55.487 --> 00:03:58.254
right, the juicy salacious details.

00:03:58.254 --> 00:04:00.902
Nobody's ever whispering small talk.

00:04:00.902 --> 00:04:05.069
Nobody's ever like, "It's a
really beautiful day out there."

00:04:06.805 --> 00:04:09.109
Why are you whispering that?

00:04:09.109 --> 00:04:11.480
No, it's always the good
stuff and I'm missing out,

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:13.967
but I can hear the first
level of whispering.

00:04:13.967 --> 00:04:16.041
You know, when somebody's
kind of whispering,

00:04:16.041 --> 00:04:18.038
but there's still some volume.

00:04:18.038 --> 00:04:20.889
I can hear that, but
every level after that,

00:04:20.889 --> 00:04:24.797
when it gets lower and
juicier, I don't hear,

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:26.767
so, I just respond to the
first part that I heard,

00:04:26.767 --> 00:04:29.283
and I end up looking like a moron.

00:04:29.283 --> 00:04:33.031
You know, like my friend came
up to me and she was like,

00:04:33.031 --> 00:04:35.281
"I was in Bermuda last week

00:04:37.628 --> 00:04:39.961
"and I cheated on my husband

00:04:42.389 --> 00:04:45.139
"with two guys at the same time,"

00:04:50.243 --> 00:04:54.410
and I was like, "I have always
wanted to go to Bermuda."

00:04:55.289 --> 00:04:58.206
(audience laughs)

